<title>CANADA: Eurocan completes Zaire acquisition.</title>
<headline>Eurocan completes Zaire acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Eurocan Ventures Ltd said on Friday that it completed its acquisition of the Tenke Fungurume copper and cobalt project in Zaire.</p>
<p>Lundin Holdings, a wholly owned subsidiary of Eurocan, now owns 55 percent of the issued shares of Tenke Fungurume Mining S.A.R.L., which holds all rights to the Tenke and Fungurume concessions, Eurocan said.</p>
<p>As a result, C$70 million was released from escrow so Eurocan could partly pay Zaire's state mining company, Gecamines, for the acquisition.</p>
<p>Eurocan recently raised C$120 million in a share issue.</p>
